From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:13:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 216/260] [ae-patch] List pop-up dialogs in browser snapshots
 and screenshot a browser pane that is off screen

browser_snapshot stopped walking at the first element that failed its
visibility check, so a modal rendered into a zero-size or display:contents
portal root never appeared in the tree. Only display:none, opacity 0 or a
zero-area box that clips its overflow now hide a subtree; an element is
listed when it is itself visible. The walk also enters open shadow roots and
same-origin iframes.

browser_screenshot called capturePage() on the conversation's view even when
the pane was not showing it. A detached WebContentsView never resolves
capturePage() on Electron 42 (the agent saw the 30 s action timeout) and a
never-attached one returns an empty image. The new aeBrowserCapture.js stages
a detached view at the bottom of the window's child views with one pixel
inside the window, captures (retrying for up to 1 s while the image is
empty), and restores it. Every capture is capped at 10 s with an error that
says to open the chat's browser pane.
